cache/
.graphify_*
# Curriculum graph (scripts/graphify_curriculum.py): regenerated on demand or in
# CI, using the local LLM -- never committed (changes on every curriculum edit).
curriculum/

# Machine-generated graph state (2026-08-11 decision, OSS-repo hygiene).
# graph.json and graph.html were ~3.5 MB EACH and are rewritten wholesale on
# every refresh, so each regeneration added that much to history permanently.
# Both are reproducible by anyone: `graphify export html` rebuilds graph.html
# from graph.json, and a full re-extract rebuilds graph.json itself.
#
# manifest.json goes with them ON PURPOSE: it is the incremental-update
# bookkeeping for graph.json ("these files are already extracted"). Committing
# it WITHOUT graph.json would be worse than committing neither -- a fresh clone
# would read a manifest claiming everything is already extracted while having no
# graph to merge into, and `--update` would find nothing to do and produce
# nothing. Keep the pair together: both ignored, both rebuilt on first run.
#
# Still committed, deliberately: GRAPH_REPORT.md (human-readable, ~100 KB),
# mentar_graph_overview.png (embedded in README.md), cost.json (a small running
# token-spend log, not a derived artifact).
graph.json
graph.html
manifest.json
